WEBVTT

00:00.430 --> 00:02.270
How're you feeling, Tomo?

00:02.270 --> 00:04.560
Top of my game, obviously!

00:06.270 --> 00:09.730
I've been through all the 
training for this marathon!

00:09.730 --> 00:10.900
Me, too.

00:10.900 --> 00:12.820
I'm gonna win this one.

00:12.820 --> 00:14.990
Oh, yeah? That's some big talk!

00:14.990 --> 00:18.160
How about the loser has to pay 
for a week's worth of drinks?

00:18.160 --> 00:20.740
Sounds good! I hope you 
don't regret that later!

00:20.740 --> 00:23.620
The girls and boys aren't 
even running the same route.

00:23.620 --> 00:25.170
Just leave them be.

00:25.830 --> 00:30.460
Hey, he's been trying to send us 
some kind of signal this whole time.

00:31.170 --> 00:33.380
<i>Watch me, Misuzu-chan!</i>

00:33.380 --> 00:36.750
<i>I'll finish this marathon for you!</i>

00:36.750 --> 00:38.390
Just leave him be.

00:38.640 --> 00:41.100
Everyone, on your marks!

00:55.150 --> 00:58.070
Great. They're all full of energy for...

00:59.830 --> 01:02.750
At least run at the very beginning!

01:02.750 --> 01:04.120
You heard her.

01:04.120 --> 01:05.790
Oh, fine.

01:15.170 --> 01:18.970
<b>How the Contest Ends</b>

01:15.880 --> 01:17.510
"How the Contest Ends."

01:23.600 --> 01:27.310
You haven't been enjoying karate 
with me lately, have you?

01:28.310 --> 01:30.110
No, that's not...

01:30.110 --> 01:31.980
It's okay. I get it.

01:32.400 --> 01:36.860
But today, you're putting all your 
strength into keeping up with me.

01:37.150 --> 01:38.320
Tomo...

01:38.320 --> 01:43.290
But no matter how hard you run, 
I'm gonna leave you behind in the end!

01:43.290 --> 01:44.240
Don't cry, okay?

01:44.240 --> 01:48.080
Bring it on! You're the 
one who better not cry!

01:52.090 --> 01:54.710
Marathons are a total drag.

01:54.710 --> 01:56.590
I'm, like, so wiped!

01:56.590 --> 01:58.630
Keep it up, everyone!

01:59.720 --> 02:01.260
Hanao-chan's cheating!

02:01.260 --> 02:02.810
Like, <i>so</i> not fair!

02:02.810 --> 02:04.260
It's perfectly fair.

02:09.100 --> 02:12.400
Wow, they've already made it this far?

02:12.400 --> 02:14.070
Impressive!

02:14.900 --> 02:16.400
I'm not letting...

02:16.400 --> 02:17.240
...anyone...

02:17.240 --> 02:19.360
...run in front of me!

02:20.860 --> 02:22.530
Why, though?! Why?!

02:22.530 --> 02:25.870
Why?!

02:32.920 --> 02:34.500
<i>This really is fun!</i>

02:34.920 --> 02:37.340
<i>I still feel the best when 
I'm competing with her!</i>

02:39.930 --> 02:43.390
<b>Girls' Turning Point</b>

02:43.640 --> 02:46.930
<i>Oh, yeah... I got so 
excited, I didn't notice.</i>

02:47.770 --> 02:50.730
<i>We weren't competing on equal 
footing to begin with...</i>

02:51.060 --> 02:52.020
<i>Huh?!</i>

02:53.020 --> 02:56.940
Hey, hang on, Tomo! You passed it!
 You just passed it!

02:56.940 --> 02:58.240
Huh? Passed what?

02:58.240 --> 03:00.280
The girls' turning point!

03:00.280 --> 03:02.700
Hah! That don't mean squat!

03:02.950 --> 03:03.660
Huh?

03:03.660 --> 03:06.370
You wanna compete with me, don't you?!

03:06.740 --> 03:07.750
Yeah...

03:08.500 --> 03:09.750
Yeah!

03:10.870 --> 03:12.460
I'm impressed, Kosuke.

03:12.880 --> 03:15.500
We're distance runners in the 
track club, and look at you.

03:16.590 --> 03:18.550
I'm feeling good today for some reason.

03:19.380 --> 03:22.510
<i>I've gotten stronger! It's clear now!</i>

03:26.350 --> 03:28.970
Those two made the turn already?

03:28.970 --> 03:30.980
Damn, that's fast! Are they human?!

03:31.640 --> 03:33.560
<i>I've got a long way to go.</i>

03:36.400 --> 03:39.650
<i>Damn it! I still can't catch up to Tomo?</i>

03:51.210 --> 03:52.330
Tomo?!

03:57.840 --> 03:59.670
You're burning up!

04:00.300 --> 04:03.050
How could you get knocked flat by a fever?

04:03.470 --> 04:06.010
Did you do something weird yesterday?!

04:06.010 --> 04:09.220
Yesterday? Yesterday...

04:09.470 --> 04:13.390
I went out to run right 
after I finished dinner...

04:13.770 --> 04:17.110
and I think I got back around 10 PM.

04:17.110 --> 04:19.110
How many hours did you run?!

04:19.110 --> 04:23.030
After that... I took a bath and went to bed...

04:23.610 --> 04:27.780
but when I woke up, 
for some reason, I was naked.

04:27.780 --> 04:29.990
I didn't do anything weird.

04:29.990 --> 04:32.910
Like hell you didn't! 
No wonder you have a fever!

04:33.620 --> 04:34.830
Hey, Tomo!

04:35.290 --> 04:36.380
Damn it!

04:36.830 --> 04:39.250
<i>What now? I don't have my phone,</i>

04:39.250 --> 04:41.760
<i>and the teacher's with the 
group a few kilometers back.</i>

04:41.760 --> 04:43.760
<i>No sign of any cars coming, either.</i>

04:44.590 --> 04:45.800
<i>What am I, dumb?!</i>

04:45.800 --> 04:47.800
<i>What's there to even think about?!</i>

04:47.800 --> 04:49.970
<i>I've got...</i>

04:50.310 --> 04:52.180
<i>this body...</i>

04:52.180 --> 04:53.770
<i>that I've been building up!</i>

05:04.450 --> 05:06.320
T-Tomo...

05:06.740 --> 05:08.950
Keep calm and listen to me.

05:08.950 --> 05:11.200
Y-You have a cold.

05:11.450 --> 05:14.540
Okay. I think <i>you</i> need to calm down first.

05:16.290 --> 05:20.040
I see. So Jun carried me back, huh?

05:20.380 --> 05:21.960
That's what I heard.

05:21.960 --> 05:24.130
I put him through a lot of trouble.

05:24.130 --> 05:26.630
And we were looking forward 
to this marathon...

05:26.630 --> 05:29.050
But he finished first, apparently.

05:29.050 --> 05:32.260
Huh?! But wasn't he carrying me?

05:32.260 --> 05:33.430
That's probably why.

05:37.520 --> 05:40.110
Tomo, should you be awake already?

05:40.110 --> 05:41.070
Jun?!

05:41.070 --> 05:42.940
I'll be going now.

05:43.440 --> 05:47.700
You almost never get sick, 
so take advantage of this.

05:47.700 --> 05:48.530
Advantage?

05:48.530 --> 05:52.450
Since you're always so strong, 
showing weakness will be effective.

05:52.450 --> 05:55.540
Depend on him for <i>everything</i>.

05:55.540 --> 05:57.670
Would you wake up already?

05:59.290 --> 06:00.920
Here's some water.

06:00.920 --> 06:02.540
Oh... Thanks.

06:05.050 --> 06:08.760
You and Misuzu are being nicer 
to me than usual today.

06:08.760 --> 06:10.090
It's throwing me off.

06:10.430 --> 06:13.930
You wouldn't know since you've 
never been badly hurt or sick,

06:14.260 --> 06:18.060
but that's what happens when 
you're too weak to even move.

06:18.060 --> 06:19.900
That's how it is, huh?

06:20.190 --> 06:22.690
Akemi-san's coming to pick you up.

06:22.690 --> 06:24.320
Can you walk, Tomo?

06:24.320 --> 06:25.280
Yeah...

06:25.820 --> 06:26.990
Actually, no.

06:26.990 --> 06:28.490
C-Carry me!

06:28.950 --> 06:29.950
Huh?!

06:29.950 --> 06:33.370
You carried me here on your back, right?

06:33.370 --> 06:36.370
I don't remember any of it, so do it again!

06:36.370 --> 06:38.210
That doesn't even make sense!

06:38.210 --> 06:40.960
C-Carry me, damn it! I'm sick here!

06:41.250 --> 06:42.960
You seem healthy to me.

06:45.050 --> 06:46.460
Okay, fine.

06:49.720 --> 06:52.760
Oh, so this is what it feels like.

06:53.100 --> 06:55.350
You've gotten a lot bigger.

06:56.140 --> 06:57.560
So have you...

06:57.560 --> 06:59.770
Me? I've what?

07:00.140 --> 07:02.600
Uh, sorry. Forget I said anything.

07:06.400 --> 07:08.860
Sorry for everything that happened today.

07:08.860 --> 07:11.410
I even ruined our contest.

07:11.410 --> 07:12.490
Don't worry about it.

07:12.990 --> 07:16.950
Whenever you're having trouble,
 of course I'm gonna help you.

07:17.120 --> 07:21.080
If you're having trouble with something,
 of course I'm gonna help you.

07:21.580 --> 07:22.620
Jun...

07:30.220 --> 07:35.720
Tomo!

07:35.720 --> 07:37.060
Her dad?!

07:37.770 --> 07:39.890
Where is Tomo?!

07:39.890 --> 07:41.770
In the car, heading for the hospital...

07:44.480 --> 07:48.030
Wait for me, Tomo!

07:46.270 --> 07:47.400
Green onions?

07:50.530 --> 07:52.860
Hey, Jun! Thanks for coming!

07:52.860 --> 07:56.700
I came to check in on you, but... 
I guess I shouldn't be surprised.

07:56.700 --> 07:59.500
I'm totally fine now!

07:59.500 --> 08:01.960
But Mom refuses to let me go outside.

08:01.960 --> 08:03.080
Obviously.

08:03.370 --> 08:05.830
I forgot to say it with 
everything going on, but...

08:06.210 --> 08:08.920
I guess... Thanks for yesterday.

08:08.920 --> 08:12.170
S-Sure... But don't be so reckle—

08:12.170 --> 08:13.050
Oh, yeah!

08:13.800 --> 08:15.590
Here. I'm returning this.

08:19.430 --> 08:20.470
This...

08:21.100 --> 08:23.060
How long can I borrow it?

08:23.940 --> 08:26.480
Until I'm a stronger man than you.

08:26.480 --> 08:27.730
When that time comes...

08:28.230 --> 08:29.860
I'll take it back!

08:29.860 --> 08:34.570
You said you'd take it back when you 
were a stronger man than me, right?

08:35.240 --> 08:39.830
You'd better not have it in your head 
that you can beat me in everything now.

08:40.080 --> 08:43.660
I won't lose to anyone on my own turf!

08:44.120 --> 08:46.540
But that goes for both of us.

08:48.170 --> 08:49.210
Right?

08:49.840 --> 08:52.460
You have a problem being 
on even footing with me?

08:54.760 --> 08:55.760
Nah.

08:56.470 --> 08:58.010
It's the best way to be.

08:59.930 --> 09:03.980
<b>To Stay Best Friends...</b>

09:00.850 --> 09:02.600
"To Stay Best Friends..."

09:03.980 --> 09:10.940
Aizawa Dojo

09:05.190 --> 09:07.400
<i>Right before we started middle school,</i>

09:08.190 --> 09:09.860
<i>I managed...</i>

09:11.190 --> 09:13.400
<i>to land a hit on Tomo for the first time.</i>

09:13.400 --> 09:14.780
Ow...

09:15.530 --> 09:17.110
I did it!

09:17.110 --> 09:19.700
I landed a hit on you! On <i>Tomo</i>!

09:19.700 --> 09:23.120
Huh... I guess you finally caught up to me.

09:23.120 --> 09:24.660
It's kinda sad.

09:24.660 --> 09:28.250
<i>Sad? Not frustrating?</i>

09:29.130 --> 09:31.630
That happened sooner than I expected.

09:31.630 --> 09:32.500
Huh?

09:32.500 --> 09:35.760
Akemi's been going on 
about it for a long time.

09:35.760 --> 09:38.470
She always says Tomo's got natural talent,

09:38.720 --> 09:42.060
that no matter what sport Tomo plays, 
no one else will stand a chance.

09:42.060 --> 09:44.180
But walking the path I walk,

09:44.180 --> 09:46.600
the path where one can't 
choose one's own opponent,

09:46.600 --> 09:49.270
won't do our child any good.

09:49.270 --> 09:51.020
<i>What does that mean?</i>

09:51.400 --> 09:54.360
<b>Entrance Ceremony</b>

09:54.360 --> 09:57.280
I finally get to go to 
the same school as Tomo!

09:57.780 --> 10:00.950
I bet he'll look awesome 
in the school uniform!

10:01.410 --> 10:02.660
Hey, Jun!

10:03.910 --> 10:05.830
We can finally go to school together!

10:06.910 --> 10:09.790
You're getting a little too 
crazy with that skirt!

10:09.790 --> 10:11.670
What kind of new start are you making?

10:11.670 --> 10:12.210
Huh?!

10:12.580 --> 10:13.300
Huh?

10:14.090 --> 10:17.630
What? Junichiro thought you were a boy?

10:17.630 --> 10:19.720
Yes, he did!

10:19.970 --> 10:23.430
I knew he was an idiot, 
but I had no idea it went <i>that</i> far.

10:23.850 --> 10:25.810
So what are you going to do?

10:26.270 --> 10:29.440
You can't just act the same around 
him as you always have, can you?

10:29.440 --> 10:31.520
Nah, I think it'll be fine!

10:31.520 --> 10:35.400
Neither of us cares about stuff 
like who's a boy or a girl!

10:35.570 --> 10:38.740
I really don't think it'll be that simple.

10:41.740 --> 10:43.620
<i>Tomo's a girl.</i>

10:43.620 --> 10:45.040
<i>Now that I think about it...</i>

10:49.500 --> 10:51.670
<i>Who wouldn't have noticed?!</i>

10:51.670 --> 10:54.420
<i>Did I just not </i>want<i> to notice?</i>

10:54.420 --> 10:55.710
<i>I can't even laugh at this.</i>

10:56.210 --> 10:57.130
Hey,

10:58.420 --> 10:59.800
Kubota-kun.

10:59.800 --> 11:02.590
You seem to be pretty close 
to Aizawa-san in Class C.

11:02.590 --> 11:03.510
You going out?

11:05.850 --> 11:08.230
<i>Right... Of course people would think that!</i>

11:13.810 --> 11:16.280
<i>I feel so awkward trying 
to get Tomo's attention.</i>

11:16.280 --> 11:20.450
Hey, Aizawa-san, are you going out 
with Kubota-kun from Class A?

11:21.280 --> 11:22.820
No way!

11:23.450 --> 11:25.780
Oh, you're not?

11:25.780 --> 11:27.370
Really?

11:27.700 --> 11:31.870
Yeah, he doesn't even see me as a girl.

11:34.080 --> 11:35.630
And then this dude...

11:35.630 --> 11:37.630
Don't talk about that!

11:38.340 --> 11:39.720
So then what happened?

11:42.470 --> 11:44.090
Hey, it's Jun!

11:44.090 --> 11:45.140
Who?

11:45.140 --> 11:46.430
Is he your friend?

11:46.430 --> 11:48.060
Since we were kids.

11:48.060 --> 11:49.390
Right, Jun?

11:54.230 --> 11:56.480
Was that bloodlust emanating from him?

11:56.480 --> 11:58.360
Scary...

12:00.030 --> 12:03.610
<i>What the heck am I doing?!</i>

12:04.030 --> 12:06.740
<i>A whole year went by, 
and I never apologized to Tomo.</i>

12:07.280 --> 12:10.830
<i>We basically ended up on 
the level of acquaintances</i>

12:11.210 --> 12:13.620
<i>who only talked to each other 
when it was necessary.</i>

12:14.290 --> 12:16.840
<i>I really wanna just make 
up with her already.</i>

12:17.540 --> 12:20.300
<i>But if her friends get the wrong idea again,</i>

12:20.300 --> 12:22.760
<i>it'll just make her feel bad.</i>

12:26.100 --> 12:27.760
Tomo again?!

12:26.600 --> 12:28.640
<i>I thought that after we 
started middle school,</i>

12:27.760 --> 12:29.100
Yeah!

12:28.640 --> 12:31.930
<i>Tomo would start to calm down a little...</i>

12:31.930 --> 12:35.100
<i>but she still shows no 
signs of slowing down.</i>

12:35.310 --> 12:38.610
<i>I can't play the games Tomo plays anymore.</i>

12:38.860 --> 12:41.240
<i>She just keeps getting stronger,</i>

12:41.240 --> 12:43.820
<i>and I don't want to just run around outside.</i>

12:44.150 --> 12:46.570
<i>What can I do to be friends with her again?</i>

12:47.620 --> 12:51.160
<i>Of course! I just need a girlfriend and—</i>

12:51.620 --> 12:54.830
<i>Nah, that wouldn't be fair to the girl.</i>

12:54.830 --> 12:58.540
<i>And it's not that easy to 
get a girlfriend, anyway.</i>

12:58.880 --> 13:01.340
<i>If only there was someone else between us...</i>

13:01.340 --> 13:03.970
<i>Someone who could slow Tomo down a little,</i>

13:03.970 --> 13:06.340
<i>who's cautious and has common sense.</i>

13:06.590 --> 13:09.890
<i>On top of that, it'd have to 
be a girl who could hang out</i>

13:09.890 --> 13:13.140
<i>with me and Tomo while fully 
understanding my situation.</i>

13:25.150 --> 13:27.660
Does lunch taste good when you eat alone?

13:27.660 --> 13:30.030
Yeah. It just went from good to gross.

13:30.620 --> 13:33.000
You always seem to be alone.

13:33.450 --> 13:36.080
Why don't you try to make friends?

13:36.080 --> 13:39.290
I'm alone because I can't make 
friends even when I try.

13:39.290 --> 13:41.340
That's a lie. You just don't want...

13:42.050 --> 13:44.050
to replace Tomo.

13:44.970 --> 13:47.010
If someone took her place,

13:47.010 --> 13:51.140
you might never get back the relationship 
you used to have with her.

13:51.560 --> 13:53.390
That's your reasoning, isn't it?

13:54.390 --> 13:57.440
I'm pretty tired of seeing 
your sulky face by now.

13:57.770 --> 13:59.400
Quit wallowing in self-pity,

13:59.860 --> 14:02.520
and just make up with Tomo already.

14:02.520 --> 14:06.360
I'm pretty sure she needs you, after all.

14:06.990 --> 14:08.070
Gundo!

14:10.370 --> 14:15.450
Gundo, would you... 
maybe try going out with me?

14:21.210 --> 14:23.130
That sounds like fun.

14:24.340 --> 14:27.590
Hey... why did you agree to go out with me?

14:28.340 --> 14:30.890
Because I figured it couldn't hurt.

14:31.850 --> 14:33.640
Do you like me?

14:33.640 --> 14:35.020
As if.

14:35.020 --> 14:37.850
And I know it's not like 
you love me, either.

14:38.140 --> 14:41.310
Well, no...

14:41.310 --> 14:43.150
I know I'm the one who asked,

14:43.150 --> 14:45.070
but is this how "going out" 
is supposed to work?

14:45.070 --> 14:46.610
It's not a problem.

14:46.610 --> 14:50.780
In the end, what matters most if you 
want to keep up a good relationship

14:51.410 --> 14:54.080
is whether or not it's in the 
interest of both parties.

14:54.950 --> 14:57.500
Huh? Your... Your hand?!

15:03.130 --> 15:04.920
<i>It's so soft!</i>

15:08.760 --> 15:11.090
I changed my mind. Can we stop now?

15:11.760 --> 15:14.100
Your hand is all sweaty and gross.

15:17.770 --> 15:20.770
Well, I'm this way, so see ya.

15:21.400 --> 15:23.060
Hold it, Junichiro.

15:23.730 --> 15:25.570
Something else you want?

15:25.570 --> 15:29.740
Yes. I want you to call me by 
my given name from now on.

15:30.070 --> 15:31.950
Your given name?!

15:31.950 --> 15:37.330
If I'm using your given name, 
but you're not using mine,

15:37.330 --> 15:39.290
will people believe we're going out?

15:39.290 --> 15:40.410
Wouldn't they?

15:40.750 --> 15:43.920
It'll just look like I have 
a one-sided crush on you.

15:43.920 --> 15:45.420
I can't deal with that.

15:47.630 --> 15:52.010
I never thought Gundo would 
actually become my girlfriend.

15:52.010 --> 15:53.220
<i>My girlfriend?</i>

15:54.350 --> 15:57.140
<i>That's right... I have a girlfriend now.</i>

15:57.600 --> 16:01.890
<i>And it's Gundo, the girl who argues 
with me every time I see her.</i>

16:05.560 --> 16:08.360
She's... my girlfriend?

16:09.150 --> 16:12.990
Sheesh... This sure has taken a weird turn.

16:13.610 --> 16:15.780
<i>I know this is a relationship</i>

16:16.450 --> 16:19.830
<i>far removed from love and romance, 
with no future at all...</i>

16:20.700 --> 16:22.710
<i>But I still feel just a bit...</i>

16:24.040 --> 16:26.840
<i>The good feelings ended there, though.</i>

16:27.460 --> 16:30.050
<i>Our first date was a bike 
ride up a mountain.</i>

16:30.050 --> 16:32.510
Well?! Awesome view, right?!

16:34.130 --> 16:35.140
View?

16:35.890 --> 16:37.550
Are you a total moron?

16:37.550 --> 16:40.390
<i>The second day, we went 
fishing at the river.</i>

16:40.390 --> 16:42.310
Put this on your hook.

16:42.310 --> 16:44.600
Ew! Keep that away from me!

16:44.600 --> 16:46.860
Ew! It's alive!

16:47.940 --> 16:49.320
Hey, Misuzu...

16:49.940 --> 16:52.070
Was today not much fun for you?

16:52.820 --> 16:54.070
Bingo.

16:54.490 --> 16:55.780
I see...

16:55.780 --> 16:58.870
<i>If I tried to spend time 
with Tomo right now,</i>

16:58.870 --> 17:02.750
<i>I'd get exactly what I got from 
these two days with Junichiro.</i>

17:03.210 --> 17:06.170
There's just no hope for me.

17:06.170 --> 17:08.170
Hey, what's wrong with you?

17:08.170 --> 17:11.800
I thought you might be able 
to do something about this...

17:12.920 --> 17:16.890
But the way you are now, you're just
 kicking her into higher gear.

17:18.550 --> 17:20.560
Hey, what's wrong, Misuzu?

17:20.560 --> 17:22.310
You seem really down.

17:22.310 --> 17:24.100
Did something happen?

17:24.100 --> 17:27.060
Yes. A lot happened.

17:27.810 --> 17:30.270
I'm sorry. I...

17:30.900 --> 17:33.990
might not be able to keep being your friend.

17:34.990 --> 17:35.700
Come on.

17:35.700 --> 17:37.990
Ow! Hey!

17:38.450 --> 17:41.700
Where are we going? 
First period's about to start!

17:41.700 --> 17:43.620
I don't care. Come with me.

17:45.080 --> 17:47.420
What are you sulking about?

17:47.420 --> 17:49.670
What do you mean, you can't 
keep being my friend?

17:49.670 --> 17:50.790
I'll knock you out!

17:50.790 --> 17:52.210
That's extortion.

17:52.710 --> 17:55.300
I mean, I have no physical strength at all,

17:55.300 --> 17:57.260
so I can't play sports with you or anything.

17:57.260 --> 17:58.680
What does that matter?!

17:59.050 --> 18:01.890
It's not like I'm running 
around every single day!

18:02.890 --> 18:05.850
Goofing around with the guys is fun,

18:05.850 --> 18:09.480
but the time I spend just being next 
to you is way more precious to me.

18:09.860 --> 18:11.860
Are you saying you don't feel the same?

18:11.860 --> 18:14.570
Where do you learn things like that?

18:14.900 --> 18:17.320
What? Did I say something weird?

18:17.740 --> 18:21.490
Why would it matter that much 
whether you're athletic or not?

18:21.490 --> 18:23.160
I mean, like...

18:23.830 --> 18:24.830
Oh, yeah!

18:24.830 --> 18:29.210
Wouldn't it be cool for an athlete and 
some kind of doctor to be friends?

18:31.880 --> 18:34.210
What's "some kind of doctor" 
supposed to mean?

18:34.630 --> 18:35.960
Don't laugh!

18:37.470 --> 18:40.720
<i>All the things I was thinking 
seem so silly now.</i>

18:42.760 --> 18:46.520
<i>I guess going out with you 
wasn't a total waste of time.</i>

18:46.850 --> 18:48.310
<i>So I'll at least...</i>

18:48.980 --> 18:51.230
<i>dump you soundly and completely.</i>

18:51.230 --> 18:53.110
Sorry, Misuzu.

18:53.110 --> 18:53.610
Huh?

18:54.320 --> 18:58.240
I know this sounds weird when I'm 
the one who asked you out, but...

18:58.240 --> 19:01.620
I feel like maybe we're not 
a good match after all.

19:01.950 --> 19:05.410
So let's just give up on going out, okay?

19:06.750 --> 19:10.420
<i>He... beat me to it!</i>

19:11.710 --> 19:13.840
Did you hear me? Hey, Misu—

19:13.840 --> 19:16.840
Never... call me "Misuzu" again.

19:16.840 --> 19:18.670
O-Okay.

19:19.340 --> 19:22.640
<i>I guess I'll have to handle this on my own.</i>

19:24.010 --> 19:28.060
<i>I'm scared to find out how she'll react 
when I talk to her after all this time,</i>

19:28.060 --> 19:29.770
<i>but I'm prepared.</i>

19:30.640 --> 19:33.230
H-Hey, Tomo.

19:33.230 --> 19:35.820
I wanted to talk to you about something.

19:41.450 --> 19:44.580
<i>I know I should be the one to talk first.</i>

19:46.290 --> 19:47.790
<i>But what do I...</i>

19:47.790 --> 19:50.000
Hey. Hey, Jun.

19:50.000 --> 19:53.080
<i>Can I just tell her how I really feel?</i>

19:53.080 --> 19:54.880
<i>But if I tell her that...</i>

19:54.880 --> 19:56.300
I just said your name.

19:56.300 --> 19:59.340
Answer me, damn it!

20:01.180 --> 20:02.930


20:02.930 --> 20:04.680
Where did that come f—

20:04.890 --> 20:10.140
Why did you just come up and 
talk to me out of the blue?

20:10.140 --> 20:12.520
After you avoided me all this time...

20:13.520 --> 20:14.940
For a whole year...

20:16.650 --> 20:18.730
I-I'm sorry!

20:18.730 --> 20:21.450
It was my fault! Please don't cry!

20:21.450 --> 20:21.860
Huh?

20:22.530 --> 20:26.240
I'm not crying, you dumbass!

20:28.040 --> 20:32.960
Why the hell were you avoiding 
me all this time? Huh?!

20:33.210 --> 20:35.210
When the school year first started,

20:35.210 --> 20:40.420
people thought you and 
I were... well... going out.

20:40.880 --> 20:44.680
So I thought being around me would 
just make things harder for you.

20:44.680 --> 20:47.430
You were worried about 
something that stupid?!

20:47.430 --> 20:48.060
Huh?

20:48.060 --> 20:51.430
If you and I both wanna be 
together like we've always been,

20:51.430 --> 20:55.150
who the hell cares what anyone else thinks?!

20:56.270 --> 20:58.940
Well? What do <i>you</i> wanna do?

20:59.650 --> 21:00.990
I want...

21:02.320 --> 21:05.610
to be with you. Just like we always have...

21:06.240 --> 21:08.080
I wanna be like that forever!

21:12.750 --> 21:15.670
S-So just be with me, then!

21:15.670 --> 21:17.500
As f-friends!

21:17.500 --> 21:20.880
Yeah! You and I are best buds forever!

21:21.380 --> 21:23.550
So let's have a lot more 
good times together,

21:23.550 --> 21:24.590
Tomo!

21:27.760 --> 21:30.750
<i>I thought we'd never change.</i>

21:32.000 --> 21:34.530
<i>I thought it'd be best if we never changed.</i>

21:35.730 --> 21:38.730
<i>But then </i>I<i> changed.</i>

21:38.730 --> 21:40.450
<i>I think she has, too.</i>

21:41.220 --> 21:46.650
<i>So I have to think of a way 
I can still be with her forever.</i>

21:47.740 --> 21:50.200
<i>First of all, I have to face her head-on.</i>

21:50.200 --> 21:51.870
What's the hold-up, Jun?

21:52.050 --> 21:54.070
C'mon, we gotta get to school!

21:55.490 --> 21:58.290
<i>Face who Tomo is now head-on...</i>

21:58.700 --> 22:00.420
<i>Head-on...</i>

22:01.820 --> 22:04.450
<i>I had a vague hunch it might be true,</i>

22:04.450 --> 22:05.880
<i>but isn't she actually...</i>

22:06.270 --> 22:08.160
<i>really cute?!</i>

22:10.800 --> 22:14.680
<i>(This behavior is suspicious)</i>

22:14.680 --> 22:18.850
<i>Hey, you know, I'm all mixed up</i>

22:18.850 --> 22:23.170
<i>It's too complicated, I'm freaking out</i>

22:23.490 --> 22:26.070
<i>I can't figure out how to 
say it, or how to read you</i>

22:23.490 --> 22:29.440
<i>(crazy, crazy, drive me crazy, and that's...)</i>

22:26.070 --> 22:28.780
<i>All this vagueness is just 
pathetic and depressing</i>

